You are acting as a Senior Principal MERN Stack Software Engineer & Solutions Architect. Your task is to build a complete, production-ready, enterprise-grade e-commerce application inspired by Myntra.

You must write production-ready, fully functional code. DO NOT omit code, write `// TODOs`, use placeholder boilerplate, or skip file contents under any circumstances.

==================================================
PROJECT GOALS & REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

1. Customer Shopping Flow Only:
   - Search & filter products
   - View product details
   - Add/Remove/Update cart items (persisted in local state/Redux)
   - Guest Checkout & Shipping Address entry
   - Secure payment via Stripe Payment Intents API + Webhook handling
   - Post-payment processing:
     * On Success: Persist Order, generate unique tracking number, trigger Nodemailer HTML email, trigger Twilio SMS, direct to Order Success page.
     * On Failure: Log failed payment, send Payment Failure email & SMS, allow direct retry payment.
   - Real-time Order Tracking page with interactive Timeline.

2. Explicit Exclusions (DO NOT IMPLEMENT):
   - User Registration / Login / JWT Authentication
   - Wishlist / Reviews / Coupons
   - Admin Panel / Product Management CRUD / Analytics

==================================================
TECH STACK & ARCHITECTURE RULES
==================================================

Frontend Stack:
- React 19 + Vite (JavaScript / ES Modules)
- React Router DOM v6+
- Redux Toolkit (Slices: product, cart, order)
- Axios (Isolated service layer with central instance/interceptors)
- Stripe React SDK (@stripe/react-stripe-js, @stripe/stripe-js)
- React Hook Form + Zod (@hookform/resolvers/zod)
- React-Toastify / Tailwind CSS / Lucide React

Backend Stack:
- Node.js + Express.js (ES Modules: `type: "module"`)
- MongoDB + Mongoose
- Stripe Node SDK
- Nodemailer + HTML Templates
- Twilio Node SDK
- dotenv + cors + helmet + express-async-handler

Backend Architecture:
- MVC + Service Layer Architecture:
  `server/src/`
  ├── config/        (db.js, stripe.js, twilio.js, nodemailer.js)
  ├── controllers/   (productController.js, orderController.js, paymentController.js)
  ├── services/      (productService.js, orderService.js, paymentService.js, emailService.js, smsService.js)
  ├── models/        (productModel.js, orderModel.js)
  ├── routes/        (productRoutes.js, orderRoutes.js, paymentRoutes.js)
  ├── middleware/    (errorMiddleware.js, validateMiddleware.js)
  ├── utils/         (generateTrackingNumber.js, apiError.js)
  ├── templates/     (orderConfirmationEmail.js, paymentFailedEmail.js)
  ├── validators/    (checkoutValidator.js)
  └── server.js

Frontend Architecture:
  `client/src/`
  ├── api/           (axiosInstance.js, productApi.js, orderApi.js, paymentApi.js)
  ├── assets/        (styles, mock Data fallback if DB empty)
  ├── components/    (Header, Footer, SearchBar, ProductCard, CartItem, AddressForm, PaymentSummary, TrackingTimeline)
  ├── pages/         (Home, ProductDetails, Cart, Checkout, Payment, Success, Failure, Tracking)
  ├── redux/         (store.js, slices/productSlice.js, slices/cartSlice.js, slices/orderSlice.js)
  ├── utils/         (formatCurrency.js, validationSchemas.js)
  ├── App.jsx
  └── main.jsx

